---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — 상장 콘텐츠 산업 248곳. (/industry)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `/workforce` 는 이름이 알려진 **14곳(15,072명)**만 본다. 같은 공시로 **248곳(68,809명)**까지
 * 넓힐 수 있는데 안 넓히고 있었다. 유명한 회사만 세면 「산업」이 아니라 「명단」이다.
 *
 * ── 우리 지면 셋이 여기서 만난다 ──────────────────────────────
 *   `/tv-exports` 방송사 수출이 65.7% → 3.8% 로 무너졌다
 *   여기        그 방송사들의 근속은 **10.33년**으로 콘텐츠 안에서 가장 길다
 *   `/workforce` 그 자리를 가져간 제작사·게임사는 근속이 짧다
 * 오래 다니는 곳에서 수출이 빠지고, 짧게 다니는 곳에서 수출이 자란다. 그대로 적는다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 순위표로 만들지 않는다 ─────────────────────────────────
 * 회사끼리 줄세우지 않는다. **조사가 나눈 업종 그대로** 묶어 나란히 놓고,
 * 상장사 전체를 기준선으로 같이 놓는다. 등수가 아니라 위치다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 사례수를 붙인다 ────────────────────────────────────────
 * 방송 12곳처럼 얇은 칸이 있다. 모든 줄에 회사 수를 박는다.
 *
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않았다. Riot Production 승인 전이다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-content-industry.json';

const TITLE = 'Korea’s listed content industry, all 248 companies';
const DESC =
  'Every listed Korean company in broadcasting, film and audio production, and publishing including '
  + 'games — 68,809 people. Average tenure, the gender split and pay, against the listed market as a whole.';

const 만 = (v: number) => v.toLocaleString('en-US');
const 백만원 = (v: number) => '₩' + (v / 1_000_000).toFixed(1) + 'm';
const pc = (v: number) => v.toFixed(1) + '%';

const 방송 = data.groups.find((g) => g.key === 'Broadcasting')!;
const 출판 = data.groups.find((g) => g.key.startsWith('Publishing'))!;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: String(data.year),
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://dart.fss.or.kr'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/industry">
  <h1>Korea’s listed content industry, counted whole</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Not the famous companies — all {data.content.n} of them. Every listed Korean company filing under
    broadcasting, film and audio production, or publishing, from the {data.year} annual reports.{' '}
    <b>{만(data.content.staff)} people.</b>
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Against the market it sits in</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Group</th><th>Companies</th><th>Staff</th><th>Avg tenure</th><th>Women</th><th>Avg pay</th><th>Company age</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.groups.map((g) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{g.key}</td>
              <td>{만(g.n)}</td><td>{만(g.staff)}</td>
              <td class="tot">{g.tenure} yr</td><td>{pc(g.female)}</td>
              <td>{백만원(g.pay)}</td><td>{g.age} yr</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr class="sum">
            <td class="nm">All content companies</td>
            <td>{만(data.content.n)}</td><td>{만(data.content.staff)}</td>
            <td class="tot">{data.content.tenure} yr</td><td>{pc(data.content.female)}</td>
            <td>{백만원(data.content.pay)}</td><td>{data.content.age} yr</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="base">
            <td class="nm">Every listed Korean company</td>
            <td>{만(data.market.n)}</td><td>{만(data.market.staff)}</td>
            <td class="tot">{data.market.tenure} yr</td><td>{pc(data.market.female)}</td>
            <td>{백만원(data.market.pay)}</td><td>{data.market.age} yr</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Every group figure is weighted by headcount, so a 3,000-person studio and a 40-person label each
      count for their own staff rather than one company one vote. The last row is the same field on the
      same filing for the whole market — it is a baseline, not a ranking.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Two things the whole-industry view shows that the famous names do not</h2>
    <div class="flip">
      <div>
        <span class="lab">Content stays about half as long</span>
        <span class="big">{data.content.tenure} yr <span class="vs">vs {data.market.tenure}</span></span>
        <span class="det">
          Across {만(data.content.n)} companies and {만(data.content.staff)} people — the same gap we found
          in the fourteen best-known firms holds for the whole industry.
        </span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="lab">And it is far more of a women’s industry</span>
        <span class="big">{pc(data.content.female)} <span class="vs">vs {pc(data.market.female)}</span></span>
        <span class="det">
          Production is {pc(data.groups.find((g) => g.key.startsWith('Film'))!.female)} women;
          publishing and games is {pc(출판.female)}. The split inside the industry is wider than the
          gap to the market outside it.
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The broadcasters are the oldest, the longest-serving — and the ones losing the export trade</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Broadcasting is {방송.n} companies with {방송.tenure} years of average tenure, the longest in
      Korean content and close to the market as a whole. Publishing and games sit at {출판.tenure}.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Set that against what those companies sell abroad. Terrestrial broadcasters were{' '}
      <b>65.7%</b> of Korea’s television exports in 2012 and <b>3.8%</b> in 2024, while independent
      producers went from 7.2% to 51.4% — <a href="/tv-exports">the thirteen-year table is here</a>.
      The export trade moved from the long-tenure companies to the short-tenure ones. The filings and
      the trade statistics are separate sources and we are placing them side by side, not claiming one
      caused the other.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>{data.sourceKo}</b> — {data.source}.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Which companies are in.</b> Every listed company whose own filed industry code is
        broadcasting, film/video/audio production, or publishing. Korean game companies file as
        publishing, which is why games sit in that row. We did not hand-pick the list.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>{data.dropped === 0 ? 'None dropped.' : `${data.dropped} company dropped.`}</b>
        {data.dropped > 0 && ' It does not report both tenure and headcount in this filing, so it cannot be weighted and is excluded rather than counted as zero.'}
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Not a ranking, and not a judgement.</b> Average tenure falls when people leave and also when
        people arrive — a company that doubles its headcount halves its average tenure without a single
        resignation. No company is named on this page for that reason.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Privately held studios are not here.</b> Several of Korea’s busiest production houses file
        no comparable disclosure, so this is the listed part of the industry and not all of it.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      Fourteen of these companies — the best-known agencies and game studios — are broken out
      individually on <a href="/workforce">the workforce page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.7rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; line-height: 1.4; }
  .sub { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .note { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .9rem 0 0; line-height: 1.6; }

  .flip { display: grid; gap: .8rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 34rem) { .flip { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .flip > div { background: var(--card); border-radius: 8px; padding: .9rem 1rem; }
  .lab { display: block; font-size: .76rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase;
         color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; }
  .big { display: block; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin: .25rem 0 .35rem;
         letter-spacing: -.01em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .vs { font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); }
  .det { display: block; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .85rem; }
  th, td { padding: .48rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right;
           white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th { font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .03em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
       font-weight: 700; }
  th:first-child, td.nm { text-align: left; white-space: normal; }
  td.tot { font-weight: 700; }
  tr.sum td { background: var(--card); font-weight: 700; }
  /* 시장 기준선은 우리 산업이 아니다 — 색을 죽여서 「비교 대상」임을 눈으로 알게 한다 */
  tr.base td { color: var(--muted); border-top: 2px solid var(--line); }

  .src ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .src li { margin: .45rem 0; }
  .src b { color: var(--ink); }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
